# Library scope

Current **0.x** scope: **Button**, **Collapsible**, **Scroll Area**, and **Accordion** (Spec Ready — no `src/package` or `src/cli` code until its component branch starts) — each headless + styled CLI + docs — shared utils (incl. **`usePresence`**), rules/skills.

Catalog components ship **both** headless and styled unless that component’s spec says headless-only or styled-only.

Internal (no docs/CLI product): **Disclosure** — Collapsible and Accordion items compose it; Content uses `@cerevialabs/ui/utils` `usePresence`. Accordion group policy stays on Accordion, not Disclosure.

**Not in scope:** Presence compound component (deleted). Lifecycle lives in `src/package/ui/utils/use-presence.ts` (no util Spec MD).

Out of scope unless PRODUCT.md changes: rest of INDEX backlog, real CLI binary, npm publish, Fallow as a CI gate (local `npm run fallow` OK).

Semver: package is `0.x` until full INDEX + CLI + package are ready → then `1.0.0`. New shipped components / meaningful library changes bump **minor** in 0.x.

Challenge scope creep. Do not scaffold new components outside Spec Ready MDs for the current 0.x scope.
